
== S0  transcription of the landed tables (read-only)
PASS S0.sgn  [source] landed sgn is -1 exactly at (1,3) and (2,2)
PASS S0.pc  [source] landed pc table
PASS S0.pt  [source] landed pt table
PASS S0.phiW  [source] landed phiW = diag(1,1,-1,1)
PASS S0.reflY  [source] landed reflY = diag(1,-1,1)
PASS S0.cnot  [witness] phiW = cnot (prodState xplus z3) (landed cnot_prodState_xplus_z3, recomputed)

== S1  token orders: which groupings a fixed order makes contiguous (exhaustive)
PASS L1  [enumerate] each of the 24 linear orders makes exactly one pairing contiguous (two adjacent blocks of two)
PASS L2  [enumerate] no linear order makes both A = 01|23 and B = 02|13 contiguous -- orders realizing A: 8, B: 8
PASS L3  [enumerate] the 24 orders give exactly 3 cyclic orders up to rotation and reflection -- [(0, 1, 2, 3), (0, 1, 3, 2), (0, 2, 1, 3)]
PASS L4  [enumerate] cyclic order 0-1-3-2 is the only one in which A and B are both non-crossing; C = 03|12 crosses there -- {(0, 1, 2, 3): ['A=01|23', 'C=03|12'], (0, 1, 3, 2): ['A=01|23', 'B=02|13'], (0, 2, 1, 3): ['B=02|13', 'C=03|12']}
PASS L5  [enumerate] the edges of the cycle 0-1-3-2-0 are exactly the four KT4 pairs 01, 23, 02, 13
PASS L6  [enumerate] the one-click rotation 0->1->3->2->0 maps the pairs of A onto the pairs of B; the transposition (12) does too
PASS L4c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: in the cyclic order 0-1-2-3, B = 02|13 crosses

== S2  the four-token table calculus (four-copy local tomography built in, as Lemma B2)
PASS B2.1  [identity] effA e f (prodA X Y) = ipW e X * ipW f Y (open sorry effA_prodA of FourCopyPackage A.2)
PASS B2.2  [identity] effB E F (prodB L L') = ipW E L * ipW F L' (open sorry effB_prodB)
PASS B2.3  [identity] effB E F (prodA X Y) = fourVal X Y E F (open sorry effB_prodA): the famI form
PASS B2.4  [identity] effA e f (prodB L L') = g2 e f L L' (open sorry effA_prodB): the famII form
PASS B2.5  [identity] W4 pairing, grouping A: <prodA X Y, prodA U V> = ipW X U * ipW Y V
PASS B2.6  [identity] W4 pairing, grouping B: <prodB X Y, prodB U V> = ipW X U * ipW Y V
PASS B2.7  [identity] W4 cross pairing: <prodA X Y, prodB L L'> = fourVal X Y L L' (states of A against states of B)
PASS B2.8  [identity] token exchange: sigma12 (prodA L L') = prodB L L' (naturality of the exchange of tokens 1, 2 on products)
PASS B2.8c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the identity map does not carry prodA L L' to prodB L L'
PASS B2.3c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: effA E F (prodA X Y) is not fourVal X Y E F (the cross form needs the other grouping)
NOTE [written] B2.W  -- Lemma B2 in both directions from B2.1-B2.4: if K4 contains prodA K01 K23 and prodB K02 K13 and every effA e f (e, f in the duals of K01, K23) and every effB E F is nonnegative on K4, then famI is effB on a prodA (B2.3) and famII is effA on a prodB (B2.4): FCC. Conversely, given FCC, K4 := {Om : effA e f Om >= 0 and effB E F Om >= 0 for all dual-cone factors} contains prodA (B2.1 and famI via B2.3) and prodB (B2.2 and famII via B2.4). So "one four-token cone that is a composite in both groupings" is FCC, each direction by its own argument (the second is the package's exists_kt4Cone_of_fourCopyCoherent).

== S3  ordered associativity is blind to the pairs 02 and 13
PASS A1  [witness] L' := actT reflY sing4 = diag(1,-1,1,-1) (the twin partner of the singlet table)
PASS A2  [witness] phiW and L' are gate images of products: phiW = cnot(prodState xplus z3), L' = cnotTw(prodState (-xplus) (-z3)), sing4 = cnot(prodState (-xplus) (-z3))
PASS A3  [witness] famI for the cones (Q3, Q3, Q3, twin): fourVal phiW phiW (phiW/4) (L'/4) = -1/8 -- value -1/8
PASS A3c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: with phiW/4 (a Q3 effect) in place of L'/4 the value is 1/4 >= 0
NOTE [written] A.W  -- membership: phiW, sing4 in Q3 and L' in twin are the landed F7-F9 facts (pauliW phiW, opW(phiW/4) and opW(actT reflY (L'/4)) are rank-one projectors); recomputed in s3. An ordered-associative structure for the order 0,1,2,3 (contiguous bracketings 01|23, 0|123, 012|3 and their sub-bracketings) reads only the tokens, the pairs 01, 12, 23 and the contiguous blocks: its definition contains no K02 or K13. The quantum chain (PSD on 2^k qubits at every block; Kronecker products of PSD matrices are PSD) satisfies it with K01 = K23 = Q3, and K02 = Q3, K13 = twin are admissible, closed and preserved by cnot, cnotTw. A3 then shows: ordered associativity together with the pair hypotheses does not imply FCC.

== S4  the pair 02 induced by an A-composite: admissible, but the induced pairs need not satisfy FCC
PASS I1  [identity] the 02-marginal of prodA X Y (unit effects on tokens 1, 3) is (X_a0 Y_c0): a product of the token marginals
PASS I1c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the product-marginal formula of I1 fails for prodB X Y (its 02-marginal is X Y_00)
NOTE [written] I.W  -- for X, Y in Q3 the columns (X_a0), (Y_c0) are nonnegative multiples of hom(marginal Bloch vector), so the 02-marginals of min_A(Q3, Q3) = cone(prodA Q3 Q3) generate SEP; the induced 02 effect cone (the dual of the marginal cone) is SEP* = maxCone (landed: maxCone is the set of tables nonnegative on all products a b^T, a, b in Lor). The same holds for 13. So the A-composite K4 = min_A(Q3, Q3) induces the admissible pairs (SEP, effects maxCone) on 02 and 13.
PASS I2  [identity] idW in maxCone: a^T idW b = a.b, symbolic (>= 0 for a, b in Lor by Cauchy-Schwarz on the tails)
PASS I3  [identity] sing4 in maxCone: a^T sing4 b = a0 b0 - a1 b1 - a2 b2 - a3 b3, symbolic (>= 0 on Lor x Lor)
PASS I4  [witness] induced-pair cross value: fourVal phiW phiW idW sing4 = -2 (A-product state; product of induced 02, 13 effects idW, sing4 in maxCone) -- value -2
PASS I4c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: with the product effect prodState z3 z3 in place of sing4 the value is >= 0 -- value 2
NOTE [written] I4.W  -- with I2, I3 (and the tail Cauchy-Schwarz) idW and sing4 lie in maxCone, the induced 02 and 13 effect cones of K4 = min_A(Q3, Q3); phiW lies in Q3, so prodA phiW phiW lies in K4. By B2.3 the value I4 is the product effect effB idW sing4 at a state of K4: the product of induced local effects is not an effect of K4. An A-composite therefore induces admissible pairs on 02 and 13 but does not make them compose (the effect side of cross-pairing fails). With K4 = PSD16 instead the induced pairs are Q3 and cross-pairing holds; the difference lies in K4, not in associativity.

== S5  the ladder (written; identities above)
NOTE [written] LAD  -- rungs for fixed admissible pair cones, four-token cone K4 in W4: (R1) K4 an A-composite, min_A <= K4 <= max_A: always satisfiable (K4 = min_A, by B2.1); ordered associativity adds only contiguous blocks (L1, L2) and never reads K02, K13 (S3). (R2) state-level cross-pairing, min_A u min_B <= K4: always satisfiable (K4 = cone(min_A u min_B)). (R3) effect-level cross-pairing, K4 <= max_A n max_B: given R2 it is exactly famI and famII (B2.3, B2.4). R2 and R3 together are FCC (B2.W). Stating R2 or R3 at all needs the token identification across groupings, i.e. the exchange of tokens 1 and 2 natural on products (B2.8); no fixed linear order supplies it (L2); in the cyclic order 0-1-3-2 both groupings are non-crossing (L4).

